-here are some uses of slashes in C++ besides creating new lines, escape sequences. They are:

1.  Code: \t
    Name: horizontal Tab
    What it does: Moves the cursor to the next tab stop(indents text)

Example:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
  cout << "Hello World \t";
  cout << "I am learning about C++";
  return 0;
}

// Ouput will be:
  Hello World 	I am learning about C++

2.  Code: \\
    Name: Backslash
    What it does:since "\" starts every escape sequence, you need "\\" to print one on screen

Example:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
  cout << "Hello World\\";
  cout << "I am learning about C++";
  return 0;
}

// Output will be:
  Hello World!\I am learning C++

3.  Code: \"
    Name: Double Quote
    What it does: Prints a quote mark (since quote end string)

Exmaple:
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
  cout << "They call me \"Luthfiansyah\".";
  return 0;
}

// Output will be:
    They call me "Luthfiansyah".

Explanation:
-  Without escape sequences, you'd hit a wall trying to print quotes, file paths, or formatted layouts. 
   They're small but essential tools whenever you work with text output.
